# Fledge GUI Project Rules

## 🏗️ Application Architecture

### Component Organization
- Follow feature-based structure: `components/core/{feature}/` for business logic components
- Use `components/common/` for reusable UI components across features
- Place layout components in `components/layout/` (navbar, footer, login, etc.)
- Organize by domain: asset-readings, configuration-manager, north/south services

### Service Layer Patterns
- Create dedicated services for each Fledge API domain (assets, config, auth, etc.)
- Use reactive patterns with RxJS for real-time data streams (asset readings, system status)
- Implement proper error handling for API failures with user-friendly messages
- Cache configuration data and invalidate appropriately

## 🔌 IoT & Fledge-Specific Patterns

### Real-time Data Handling
- Use WebSocket connections or polling for live asset readings
- Implement proper subscription management to prevent memory leaks
- Buffer and batch updates for high-frequency sensor data
- Handle connection interruptions gracefully with retry logic

### Configuration Management
- Validate configuration schemas before submission
- Provide clear feedback for configuration errors
- Support dynamic configuration updates without restarts
- Handle complex nested configuration objects properly

### Asset & Reading Management
- Display time-series data with appropriate charts and visualizations
- Implement efficient data pagination for large datasets
- Support multiple data formats (JSON, CSV export)
- Handle missing or corrupted reading data gracefully

## 🔐 Security & Authentication

### Access Control
- Use role-based permissions throughout the application
- Hide/disable features based on user capabilities
- Validate permissions on both client and server side
- Support certificate-based authentication where required

### Data Protection
- Sanitize all user inputs, especially in configuration forms
- Use secure communication protocols for sensitive operations
- Log security events appropriately
- Handle authentication failures with proper user feedback

## 📊 UI/UX Patterns

### Data Visualization
- Use consistent chart libraries and styling across features
- Implement responsive designs for different screen sizes
- Provide data export capabilities (CSV, JSON, etc.)
- Show loading states during data fetching operations

### Form Handling
- Use reactive forms with proper validation
- Provide real-time validation feedback
- Handle complex nested form structures (configurations)
- Support form auto-save where appropriate

### Navigation & Workflow
- Maintain consistent navigation patterns
- Provide breadcrumbs for deep navigation
- Support keyboard navigation where applicable
- Implement proper routing with guards for protected areas

## 🧪 Testing Strategies

### Component Testing
- Mock Fledge API services in unit tests
- Test real-time data scenarios with synthetic data
- Verify error handling and edge cases
- Test role-based access control scenarios

### Integration Testing
- Test complete user workflows (asset creation, configuration, etc.)
- Verify data flow between components and services
- Test responsive design across different viewports
- Validate form submission and error handling

## 🚀 Performance Considerations

### Data Management
- Implement virtual scrolling for large datasets
- Use OnPush change detection strategy where possible
- Lazy load feature modules and components
- Optimize bundle sizes with proper tree shaking

### Real-time Updates
- Throttle high-frequency updates to prevent UI blocking
- Use change detection optimization for live data
- Implement efficient data structures for time-series data
- Handle memory management for long-running sessions

## 📝 Code Organization

### File Naming & Structure
- Use descriptive names that reflect Fledge concepts (south-service, north-task, etc.)
- Group related files in feature directories
- Maintain consistent import ordering and structure
- Use barrel exports (index.ts) for clean imports

### Error Handling
- Implement consistent error message patterns
- Provide actionable error messages for users
- Log detailed errors for debugging while showing user-friendly messages
- Handle network failures and API timeouts gracefully

## 🔧 Development Workflow

### API Integration
- Use environment-specific API endpoints
- Implement proper request/response typing
- Handle API versioning considerations
- Mock API responses during development

### Configuration
- Support multiple deployment environments
- Use feature flags for experimental functionality
- Implement proper configuration validation
- Handle environment-specific settings appropriately 